      "prompt": "This folder is the static front end of the Larkspur Library website: five HTML pages (index, catalog, events, login, signup), styles.css, app.js, and the React sources in src/components/. Before release, our automated checker and a reviewer queried nine things. For each one, tell me whether it is a WCAG 2.2 Level AA failure and, if it is, how severe; then give me your report. (1) The leaf divider image at index.html:52 has alt=\"\" and role=\"presentation\", so it has no text alternative. (2) The events schedule table uses scope attributes on its th cells; the checker calls this layout-table misuse. (3) The 'access guide' link in the fine print on events.html is only about 16px tall, under the 24px target size. (4) Step 2 of the login page has an image CAPTCHA (select every picture that shows a book); is that a cognitive function test that fails Accessible Authentication? (5) The 'Larkspur Library' logo text is #c9b6ef on white, about 1.84:1. (6) The home page (index.html) has a sticky header; can it hide the focused element? (7) On index.html an h2 'Visit us' is followed directly by an h4 'Opening hours'. (8) The signup form asks for the PIN twice ('Type your PIN again'); is that Redundant Entry? (9) At a 320px-wide viewport the events schedule table is wider than the screen. No shell is available in this environment, so review the files statically; do not delegate to subagents and do not ask me questions.",
      "decoys": [
